## Errors & Mistakes
Commit a514c57 routed every PreTrainedModel fallback through the new raw writer. It also retried the same custom hook with model.state_dict after any FULL_SHARD failure, which could silently emit a sharded artifact and could leave peer ranks blocked if rank zero failed again.

## Dead Ends
Restoring the original PR's broad generic synchronization rewrite was rejected because it changed rank selection and error policy for every draft model. Leaving the inherited final barrier for custom-schema failures was rejected because a rank-zero-only transformation error can deadlock peers.

## Hints for Future Agents
The custom-schema path uses the Gloo group to exchange Python error strings. A successful custom-schema save returns after the all-gather, which is the required synchronization point. Models without config_for_serving or state_dict_for_serving retain the upstream behavior exactly.

## Codebase Discoveries
FULL_SHARD get_model_state_dict must succeed before a DFlash2 online serving artifact is valid. A replicated model may safely use model.state_dict as a fallback, but a sharded model must fail closed. Model-specific artifact transformation happens only on rank zero, so its errors must still be propagated to all ranks.

